# Keep the Cloud Build upload context tight (Docker build itself uses .dockerignore).
.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.env
.local
data/raw
*.log
.claude
.superpowers
founder-outputs

# Build output and deploy caches for the OTHER deployable in this repo. The
# image built here is the API; the Next.js app ships to Firebase Hosting and
# nothing in the Dockerfile reads any of these. .dockerignore already drops
# .next, but that runs after the upload, so the bytes still crossed the wire.
# .next-check is the same output under another name (`build:check` sets
# NEXT_DIST_DIR so a production build cannot clobber a running dev server), so
# it needs its own line: 138 MB of webpack cache that no glob for .next catches.
.next
**/.next
.next-check
**/.next-check
.firebase

# Git worktrees live inside the repo, so an unignored one uploads a second full
# checkout (1.5 GB when this was written) that the build then throws away.
.worktrees
